# claim_preserve_witness.rish — safety that makes a broad Radiant pass honest.
# Missing Rishi verb (this wrapper's body): accumulate · filter chained · read bounded — counsel 20260725.040247
#
# For every file a pass touches, extract claim tokens (numbers · hex digests ·
# key fingerprints · file paths · stamps · capitalized proper nouns) BEFORE and
# AFTER, and assert the sets are identical. Modality counts (must · should · may ·
# recommend · require · seat · hold · parked · …) must match too — token identity
# misses a shifted obligation, which is the drift that would hurt a tree of
# proposals and holds. Also asserts known pinned digests did not move.
# Any mismatch → STOP; do not "resolve."
#
# Seated 20260724.222620 · Quin relay.
#
#   CLAIM_PRESERVE_FILES=$'a.md\nb.md' rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cl/claim_preserve_witness.rish
#
# Vacuous self-check (no files) fails closed — a pass must name its surface.

say "claim_preserve: token identity + modality + pinned digests + markdown structure…"
let scan = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/fixtures/claim_preserve_scan.rish"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "claim_preserve RED — STOP the wave"
let md = run ["rishi/bin/rishi" "run" "tools/fixtures/markdown_structure_scan.rish"]
say md.out
assert md.ok else "markdown_structure RED — STOP the wave"
say "GREEN: claim_preserve — tokens and modality identical; pins held; structure held."
